        "artifact_version_id": "artifact_fraud_thresholds_v1",
        "chunk_id": "chunk_263c1efc696278c373213f16",
        "content": "# Fraud scoring thresholds (synthetic, restricted) Owner: Risk Engineering. Classification: restricted. The transaction risk model returns a score from 0 to 1000. Current production thresholds are approve below 620, step-up challenge from 620 to 819, and decline at 820 and above. Thresholds are tuned monthly against the trailing chargeback cohort. Threshold values are restricted. Publishing them, including in incident notes or merchant correspondence, allows an adversary to size transactions to sit below the challenge boundary. Support staff may state that a transaction was challenged or declined by risk controls; they may not state the score or the boundary. A routing or availability incident does not change these thresholds. Lowering a threshold to clear a backlog requires Risk Engineering sign-off and is never an incident-time action.",
        "content_checksum": "sha256:fb738cb685a777289343d221af33d28248bb296bab281f784ed019b9558feb68",
        "fused_rank": 8,
        "fused_score": 0.02877846790890269,
        "lexical_rank": 10,
        "lexical_score": 19.0,
        "position": {
          "kind": "section",
          "locator": "thresholds"
        },
        "provenance_checksum": "sha256:dfef41d2c03b05e6d2a46a6a0e4c881395e4598324792d2a7d7180b620d80607",
        "rerank_rank": 10,
        "rerank_score": 0.3333333333333333,
        "title": "Fraud scoring thresholds",
        "vector_rank": 9,
        "vector_score": 0.35276684147527876
      },
      {
        "artifact_id": "artifact_rate_limit_policy",
        "artifact_version_id": "artifact_rate_limit_policy_v1",
        "chunk_id": "chunk_03bcc2c7f755f447d2a3d325",
        "content": "# Public API rate limit policy (synthetic) Owner: Developer Platform. Classification: public. Sandbox keys are limited to 10 requests per second per key with a burst allowance of 30. Production keys are limited to 200 requests per second per merchant account with a burst of 500. Limits are enforced per merchant account, not per key, so rotating keys does not raise a ceiling. Requests over the limit return HTTP 429 with a Retry-After header in whole seconds. Clients are expected to honor Retry-After and apply exponential backoff with jitter. Retrying a 429 without backoff is the single most common cause of a merchant remaining throttled. Rate limiting is independent of authorization outcomes. A throttled request was never routed to an acquirer and must not be treated as a decline.",
        "content_checksum": "sha256:d93d413404f9f6e2e50364977efec96241f162522b1a315bdca3b8650744e2bc",
        "fused_rank": 10,
        "fused_score": 0.015151515151515152,
        "lexical_rank": 6,
        "lexical_score": 21.0,
        "position": {
          "kind": "section",
          "locator": "limits"
        },
        "provenance_checksum": "sha256:9572b2366685ee087f632f70aa3f5cd67b1b8efdf88fec4d728b28fa913c0d18",
        "rerank_rank": 11,
        "rerank_score": 0.3333333333333333,
        "title": "Public API rate limit policy",
        "vector_rank": null,
        "vector_score": null
      },
      {
        "artifact_id": "artifact_prior_incident_0987",
        "artifact_version_id": "artifact_prior_incident_0987_v1",
        "chunk_id": "chunk_6dec7272256cf17edffb90ae",
        "content": "{\"error_code\":\"STL-208\",\"incident_id\":\"INC-0987\",\"not_related_to\":\"issuer routing or authorization decline handling\",\"opened_at\":\"2026-05-12T03:40:00Z\",\"resolution\":\"Deduplicated by acquirer reference and added a unique constraint. The worker now upserts on the reference key.\",\"resolved_at\":\"2026-05-12T09:15:00Z\",\"root_cause\":\"The reconciliation worker used a non-idempotent insert keyed on a timestamp rather than the acquirer chargeback reference.\",\"route\":\"Settlement Engineering\",\"service\":\"settlement-worker\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"summary\":\"A reconciliation job retried after a partial write and created duplicate chargeback rows for 1,412 synthetic transactions. Merchant balances were overstated for six hours.\",\"tenant\":\"HelioPay (fictional)\",\"title\":\"Duplicate chargeback records after reconciliation retry\"}",
        "content_checksum": "sha256:f0f8a6bf978b8ea74083aecc30296866119fa56a07bc41bbb0bdc5ba81a5da54",
        "fused_rank": 11,
